<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="stuffed-leaves" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Stuffed Grape Leaves</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>1 recipe <xref ref="greek-rice">Greek Rice Pilaf</xref></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Approximately 24 grape leaves</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>10 \frac{1}{2}</m> ounces silken tofu</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>2 tablespoons lemon juice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon salt</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Preheat oven to <m>325^\circ</m> F.  Lightly oil a baking tray.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Place each leaf down flat on a clean surface.  Add a heaping tablespoon of filling near the stem end.  Roll tightly, folding in the sides.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Arrange the stuffed leaves on the prepared tray.  Bake about 20 minutes or until heated through.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          While the stuffed leaves are baking, place the remaining ingredients in a blender or food processor and whip.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Serve the sauce in a side dish.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>